% nvim, neovim, keymaps, keys, vim

; Built-in Vim keys (no description in your config, so not in the generated
; keymaps sheet). Lookup only: in Neovim, press the key yourself.

# Jump back to where you were (after gd, a search, a jump)
Ctrl-O

# Jump forward again
Ctrl-I

# Change the word under the cursor
ciw

# Change inside quotes
ci"

# Delete inside brackets
di(

# Delete a word and its space
daw

# Change inside braces
ci{

# Delete a paragraph
dap

# Repeat the last change
.

# Search for the word under the cursor
*

# Next / previous search match
n

# Undo / redo
u

# Redo
Ctrl-R

# First / last line of the file
gg

# Last line of the file
G

# First non-blank / end of line
^

# End of line
key $

# Matching bracket
key %

# Find a character in the line (repeat with ; and ,)
f

# Select lines / characters / a block (columns)
V

# Visual block selection
Ctrl-V

# Reselect the last selection
gv

# Indent / unindent the selection
>

# Uppercase the selection
U

# Jump to the last change
key `.

# Next / previous changed block in a diff
]c

# Leave terminal typing mode (Claude, terminals)
Ctrl-\ Ctrl-N

# Close every other window
Ctrl-W o

# Make all windows the same size
Ctrl-W =

# Change inside the nearest quotes of any kind (mini.ai)
ciq

# Change inside the nearest brackets of any kind (mini.ai)
cib

# Change inside the NEXT quotes on the line (mini.ai)
cinq

# Change inside the LAST/previous brackets (mini.ai)
cilb

# Delete a function argument and its comma (Treesitter)
daa

# Change inside the function body (Treesitter)
cif

# Select the whole function (Treesitter)
vaf

# Surround the word with quotes (nvim-surround)
ysiw"

# Surround the whole line with brackets (nvim-surround)
yss)

# Change surrounding single quotes to double (nvim-surround)
cs'"

# Change surrounding brackets to square ones (nvim-surround)
csb]

# Delete surrounding brackets (nvim-surround)
ds(

# Delete surrounding quotes of any kind (nvim-surround)
dsq

# Wrap the visual selection in a tag (nvim-surround, visual mode)
gst

# In Oil: go up a folder (edit lines to rename/delete/move files, then :w)
-

# In grug-far (find and replace): replace everywhere
,r

# In grug-far: write your edits to result lines back to the files
,s
